<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-lognormal-workup> {
  ex:lg-process a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-process-h, ex:lg-process-c, ex:lg-process-v ; cd:narration "Continue immediately from additive normal errors, but explicitly change analyte and method. We now discuss an organic trace analyte by LC-MS/MS in ng/L. A repeats injection of one already prepared solution; B independently repeats the complete procedure on aliquots from one homogeneous sample. They do not measure between-site environmental variation. A hypothetical multiplicative candidate model may suit B, but preparation alone does not guarantee lognormality. Return to how the procedure acts on a result before naming the new law."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-process-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Two different repeat experiments"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-process-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-process-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-process-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-process-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-process-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-process-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-data a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-data-h, ex:lg-data-t ; cd:narration "Compare the supplied ten illustrative outcomes in ng/L, not real validation data. The two columns are separate, unpaired series; the preparation column is sorted for display and its row number does not imply acquisition order. A few large positive results in B invite questions about mechanism, not automatic rejection as outliers. Ten values neither establish a distribution nor determine the parameters of our later teaching model. Expand to a simulated experiment next, retaining that distinction."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-data-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "What could explain these large preparation results"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-data-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-data-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-data-t a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-table ; cd:communicativeRole cd:TableRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasTableRow" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-compare-live a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-compare-h, ex:lg-compare-p, ex:lg-compare-code-item ; cd:narration "Optional instructor demonstration of separate instrument and full-preparation experiments. The code openly specifies its generating assumptions, rather than fitting the ten illustrative values. Normal log factors produce an exact lognormal product in this simplified model. Binary log factors remain a finite discrete product and can illustrate an approximation as the number of log contributions grows. Histograms have the same concentration units but different panel ranges; do not compare their bar heights as point probabilities. No theoretical overlay is needed to ask why B is right-skewed."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-compare-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Repeat both procedures one thousand times"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-compare-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-compare-p a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-task ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ExerciseRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-compare-code-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-saved a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-h, ex:lg-saved-v ; cd:narration "The static fallback publishes all thousand preparation outcomes as exact bin counts, not artificial midpoint observations. It replays the default three independent normal-log-factor protocol with seed 20261103. A right tail appears under those assumptions. The hundred exceedances above fifteen in this realization are a finite simulated frequency, not the exact population probability derived later. Return from the picture to the physical mechanism: absolute steps or relative factors?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-saved-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Why the long right tail"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-saved-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-saved-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-saved-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-saved-chart ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-effects-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-effects-h, ex:lg-effects-f ; cd:narration "Compare equal absolute deviations with reciprocal relative changes. Ten plus or minus two gives eight and twelve. Ten times reciprocal factors 0.8 and 1.25 gives eight and twelve point five. The factors undo each other, but the absolute offsets are unequal. This is why a ratio is a natural comparison for a multiplicative process. Relative factors can be defined around a reference procedure; they are not unbounded physical extraction-recovery fractions."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-effects-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Additive steps or multiplicative ratios"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-effects-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-effects-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-effects-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-effects ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-factor-live a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-factor-h, ex:lg-factor-p, ex:lg-factor-code-item ; cd:narration "Make the mechanism the main experiment, not a decorative preface to a density formula. Apply an editable sequence of reciprocal factors to the same starting scale. Three factors of 1.25 give 19.53125 ng/L; three of 0.8 give 5.12. Matching one factor with its reciprocal returns to the previous value. Plot both the concentration path and its log ratio, so equal log steps can be compared with unequal absolute steps. Instructor operation is optional; no mandatory reveal or audience programming is needed."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-factor-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Apply a factor, then its reciprocal"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-factor-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-factor-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-factor-p a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-factor-task ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ExerciseRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-factor-code-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-factor-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-scale-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-log-scale-h, ex:lg-log-scale-v, ex:lg-log-scale-f ; cd:narration "Use exactly the same three concentrations on both axes. Their linear gaps are two and two point five ng/L. Their natural log ratios to ten are opposite values about 0.22314 apart from zero. The logarithm follows the ratio model, not a desire to force any skewed histogram into normality. All arguments are dimensionless; negative log ratios are valid even though concentrations must remain positive."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-scale-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Same concentrations, different distance scales"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-scale-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-log-scale-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-scale-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-scales-media ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-scale-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-log-scale ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-product-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-product-h, ex:lg-product-c, ex:lg-product-f ; cd:narration "Logarithms turn products into sums. This reconnects the mechanism to the normal lecture: independent normally distributed log contributions sum to a normal log ratio exactly. More general many-small-contribution arguments require finite variances and suitable independence or dependence conditions, and give an approximation rather than a universal law. A finite product of binary factors remains discrete. Positive support and multiplication alone do not prove lognormality."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-product-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Logarithms turn the product into a sum"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-product-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-product-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-product-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-factor-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-product-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-product ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-definition-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-definition-h, ex:lg-definition-f ; cd:narration "Define lognormality through a normal natural-log ratio. Exponentiating a normal variable and restoring the reference concentration gives a positive, right-skewed concentration. The distribution is exact under this assumed normal log model; earlier general CLT arguments only motivated an approximation. Fix reference ten ng/L, log mean zero and log SD 0.30 for the main calculations, independently of the ten illustrative outcomes."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-definition-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Exponentiating a normal log ratio creates the model"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-definition-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-definition-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-definition-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-definition ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-transform-live a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-transform-h, ex:lg-transform-p, ex:lg-transform-code-item ; cd:narration "Generate normal log ratios and transform the same values, not a new unrelated sample. Compare log SD 0.15, 0.30 and 0.60 with a fixed median of ten. Increasing log spread stretches the positive upper tail and moves arithmetic expectation to the right. The third panel shows density curves only up to thirty-five ng/L; probabilities and population moments are calculated from the full model. The following center formulas and values provide a static alternative."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-transform-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Keep the median fixed and increase log spread"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-transform-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-transform-p a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-task ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ExerciseRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-transform-code-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-centers-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-centers-h, ex:lg-centers-c, ex:lg-centers-f ; cd:narration "Unlike a normal model, mode, median and arithmetic expectation do not coincide. For positive log SD the mode is smaller than the median, which is smaller than the mean. At log SD 0.30 and median ten, the model values are about 9.14, 10.00 and 10.46 ng/L. Rare large concentrations pull arithmetic expectation upward. These are population quantities under the specified model, not summaries fitted from the ten-row illustration."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-centers-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Mode, median and mean no longer coincide"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-centers-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-centers-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-centers-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-centers-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-centers-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-centers ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-geometric-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-geometric-h, ex:lg-geometric-c, ex:lg-geometric-f ; cd:narration "Recall the geometric mean from the earlier mean-values lecture, now written with dimensionless log ratios. It is the exponential of the average log ratio multiplied by the reference concentration, and is invariant to the chosen fixed reference. For a lognormal population its population target equals the median; the sample estimator is not claimed unbiased. Choose a scientific target rather than declaring geometric averaging universally better. Mean amount per equal volume uses arithmetic expectation; a multiplicative center can use the median or geometric mean. A median matching a nominal target does not establish arithmetic unbiasedness."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-geometric-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Which center answers our analytical question"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-geometric-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-geometric-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-geometric-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-target-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-geometric-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-geometric ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-functions-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-functions-h, ex:lg-functions-f ; cd:narration "Reuse the preceding normal tools rather than inventing new density and probability functions. Standardize the natural log ratio, not the original concentration. Since the transformation is monotone, the concentration CDF is uppercase Phi at z L. Differentiating introduces the chain-rule factor one over x times log SD; this restores the density's reciprocal concentration units. Density height is still not a probability. For nonpositive concentrations the lognormal CDF and density are zero, and the log argument is not evaluated."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-functions-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "The same phi and Phi, with a log-scale z-score"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-functions-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-functions-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-functions-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-functions ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-tail-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-tail-h, ex:lg-tail-f ; cd:narration "Return to the hypothetical LC-MS/MS method under median ten ng/L and log SD 0.30. The threshold fifteen gives z L about 1.35155036 and exact upper model probability 0.0882595996, about 8.83 percent. This is not the probability of method failure or the finite frequency from one simulation. The saved default experiment had a hundred of a thousand exceedances; finite random frequencies differ from the model probability. Fifteen is an illustrative upper control threshold, not a legal limit or release criterion."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-tail-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "How often would a stable model exceed 15 ng/L"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-tail-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-tail-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-tail-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-tail ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-quantile-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-quantile-h, ex:lg-quantile-f ; cd:narration "Reverse the question exactly as in the normal section. A five-percent upper-tail target uses the 95th standard-normal percentile on the log-ratio scale. Convert that threshold back by exponentiating and multiplying by the reference concentration. The unrounded concentration threshold is 16.3796740847 ng/L, displayed about 16.38. It is a per-result model quantile, not an operational limit. Multiple checks, parameter estimation, reporting resolution and control-rule authorization remain separate questions."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-quantile-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Find an upper threshold for a five-percent tail"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-quantile-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-quantile-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-quantile-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-quantile ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-environment-live a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-environment-h, ex:lg-environment-p, ex:lg-environment-code-item ; cd:narration "Explicitly switch populations from repeated analyses of one homogeneous sample to concentrations at one hundred river sites. The demonstration has separate site log SD 0.60, not the method log SD 0.30. Linear and log histograms use the same retained data, and a normal Q-Q plot can reveal departures on the log scale. Mixtures can invalidate a single lognormal model. In censored mode, record non-detects as missing with their threshold and print a warning that detected-only plots are selected data. Never substitute zero and take its logarithm. The simplified generator is independent; actual sites may be spatially dependent."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-environment-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "New population: one hundred river sites"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-environment-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-environment-p a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-task ; cd:communicativeRole cd:ExerciseRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-environment-code-item a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-code ; cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-checks a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-checks-h, ex:lg-checks-c ; cd:narration "The model is not established by positive support, right skew or a roughly straight Q-Q plot. Different loading sources, mixture populations and dependence can need different models. Between-site variation is not analytical repeatability. Censoring below a quantification threshold carries information; zeros cannot simply be logged and excluding censored results also biases the retained sample. Use an appropriate censored-data analysis and domain knowledge rather than pretending the log transform solves every problem."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-checks-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Positive and right-skewed does not prove lognormal"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-checks-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-checks-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-checks-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-check-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-variance-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-log-variance-h, ex:lg-log-variance-f ; cd:narration "Preview the question to be derived next: a variance estimate is random even on the normal log-ratio scale. Under independent identically normal uncensored log ratios, the scaled log variance has the chi-square reference. This is not a law for raw lognormal concentration variance and cannot be transferred uncritically to correlated river sites or censored observations. We will construct the reference through independent normal squares in the following nitrate precision story, then can transfer it back to suitable log ratios."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-variance-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Next problem: the estimated log spread is random"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-variance-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-log-variance-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-log-variance-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-log-variance ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-bridge a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-bridge-h, ex:lg-bridge-c ; cd:narration "The combined story is now additive normal processes, multiplicative lognormal processes, then uncertainty of estimated spread. Explicitly return from ng/L trace-analyte workup to the separate nitrate IC example in mg/L. There the normal-error precision check constructs chi-square from squared standardized residual coordinates. It is not a test on the raw concentration variance of the LC-MS/MS lognormal model. Earlier known-parameter probability examples do not establish actual method precision or absence of bias."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-bridge-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "From a distribution model to uncertain precision"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-bridge-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-bridge-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:lg-bridge-c a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:lg-bridge-cards ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
